# PLAN-827 V-07 formal face: the SAME AP-01 source through TWO checks of
# one session — every check spawns a NEW worker process; the session id
# shares one warm store across those processes (the parent owns cleanup).
# Check 1 warms (fresh, value 0); check 2 is the overlay edit
# (`return 0` -> `return 9`, exactly-once literal, validated worker- AND
# parent-side) executed by a NEW worker over the warm store, judged
# parent-side against the NEW independent expected 9. A hit is never a
# cached PASS: both runs really execute AV and the parent re-derives the
# post-edit source hash before accepting any result.

```test-case
case {
  schema: "autolang.case/2"
  id: "av.source.session-overlay"
  tags: ["av-source-827", "probe", "cache"]
  links: ["PLAN-827"]
  source: { file: "src/p-gcd-euclid.at", syntax: "auto", path: "main.at" }
  entry: { mode: "program" }
  checks: [
    { id: "warm-run", adapter: "probe", action: "run",
      options: {
        recipe: "ac-av/core-run-v1",
        av: { entry: "d_main", session: "av827-overlay" },
        steps: [ { op: "run" } ]
      },
      expect: { completion: "success", exit: 0 } },
    { id: "overlay-edit-run", adapter: "probe", action: "run",
      options: {
        recipe: "ac-av/core-run-v1",
        av: { entry: "d_main", session: "av827-overlay" },
        steps: [
          { op: "edit-source", from: "return 0", to: "return 9" },
          { op: "run" }
        ]
      },
      expect: { completion: "success", exit: 9 } }
  ]
}
```
